# Bandit configuration for prei
# See https://bandit.readthedocs.io/en/latest/config.html
#
# NOT CURRENTLY USED: bandit 1.8.0 is broken on Python 3.14 — it throws
# AttributeError on ast.Constant.s/.n (removed compat aliases) and silently
# skips almost every file, reporting a false "No issues identified"
# (see PyCQA/bandit#1219, still open). Bandit was removed from CI
# (.github/workflows/ci-quality.yml) and pre-commit (.pre-commit-config.yaml)
# for this reason. Ruff's S rule family (.ruff.toml) is the active
# security-lint gate and mirrors the skip list below. Reconsider
# reintroducing bandit once upstream ships confirmed 3.14 support.
# Tracked in docs/issues/tech-debt-bandit-python314.md.

# Skip rules that flag safe patterns used intentionally in this project:
#   B101: assert_used — pytest uses assert in tests; not production code
#   B105/B106: hardcoded_password — "Pass" is a verdict label, testpass123 is test data
#   B110: try_except_pass — intentional config fallback to defaults
#   B112: try_except_continue — intentional skip of individual property scoring
#         errors without crashing the list view
#   B310: urlopen — used for known trusted external data source (HUD)
#   B311: random — used for web scraping delays, not crypto
#   B324: hashlib — MD5 used for cache key generation only, not security
#   B105/B106: hardcoded_password — removed in Bandit 1.8+ (consolidated into B107)
skips: [B101, B110, B112, B310, B311, B324]
